pve-tools (2.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Drop the troubleshooting-image tooling from pve-tools (backward-incompatible
    removal, hence the major version bump):
    - Remove pve-create-tshoot-image (the ReaR-based restore-ISO builder).
    - pve-create-tshoot-livecd moves to the obs-network-tools repository as
      create-network-tshoot-livecd — a distro-independent, boot-only cabling
      diagnostics LiveCD built with live-build instead of a PVE cloud-init
      template. It no longer belongs in the Proxmox-specific toolset.
    Both tools did physical-host cabling diagnostics and are better maintained
    alongside the network-tools packaging pipeline (nic-xray, switch-xray).

