pve-tools (1.15.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * pve-create-tshoot-image 1.4.1: support Ceph/RBD-backed templates and
    honour -s/--storage. The offline libguestfs steps (virt-cat,
    virt-customize, virt-copy-out) were handed the raw `pvesm path` result,
    which for Ceph is a QEMU rbd: drive string libguestfs cannot open, so
    distro detection failed with a misleading "is this a Linux template?".
    A new disk_open/disk_close layer maps the RBD image to a /dev/rbdN block
    device for each offline step and unmaps it afterwards (the cleanup trap
    releases it on any exit path); file-based storage is used verbatim.
    qm clone now passes --storage, so -s is actually honoured instead of
    silently inheriting the template's storage — the two compose, with
    -s local cloning onto file storage read directly and a Ceph pool
    triggering the mapping. rbd map failures now surface their real error
    instead of being swallowed, and the --help output no longer prints raw
    escape sequences (colours use ANSI-C quoting so they render through cat
    heredocs as well as echo -e).

 -- Ciro Iriarte <ciro.iriarte+software@gmail.com>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 12:55:14 -0500

pve-tools (1.14.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * pve-import-cloud-images 1.5.0: add --max-versions and per-release pinning.
    -N/--max-versions exposes the discovery limit (how many releases each
    distribution family offers, default 2) so older releases beyond the two
    newest can be surfaced. -r/--release pins specific release(s),
    comma-separated (e.g. 22.04 or 22.04,20.04): it widens discovery so the
    requested version is not truncated away, then filters the catalog to the
    matching versions. Tokens match on version boundaries, so '10' matches
    point releases like 10.0. Combine with --distro to target one family.

 -- Ciro Iriarte <ciro.iriarte+software@gmail.com>  Fri, 14 Aug 2026 12:16:40 -0300

pve-tools (1.13.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * pve-build-windows-template 1.5.0: add an addon facility for installing
    extra software into Windows templates. --addons / --addon stage
    operator-supplied installers onto the answer ISO; each addon.conf declares
    a type (msi, exe, copy or script) that runs in the build VM after the core
    payloads and before sysprep. An addon may also ship an optional firstboot
    script, which is baked into Cloudbase-Init's LocalScripts and runs once per
    clone so software needing a per-instance identity (an AV or inventory agent
    enrolling with its own name/token) initialises itself at deployment time.
    Binaries are never downloaded or bundled: the operator supplies them, the
    same stance as --iso, and in remote mode the addon directories are copied
    to the node. A required=1 addon aborts the build on failure; the default is
    advisory. Ships worked examples under samples/addons (7-Zip silent MSI,
    Sysinternals file-copy with PATH, and a two-phase Wazuh agent that enrols
    per clone) plus samples/ci-userdata-chocolatey.yaml for the clone-time
    package-manager route via Cloudbase-Init user-data.

 -- Ciro Iriarte <ciro.iriarte+software@gmail.com>  Thu, 06 Aug 2026 10:45:00 -0300

pve-tools (1.12.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * pve-build-windows-template 1.4.0: put the locale in the template name.
    The name was ci-win<release>-<sku>-<edition>-<timestamp>, so two
    localisations of the same release, SKU and edition were separated only
    by the timestamp, which has minute resolution and is taken once per
    run. Concurrent builds therefore collided outright: a 2019 en-US and a
    2019 ja-JP build started seconds apart both sealed as
    ci-win2019-std-core-202608051606.x86-64. Names are now
    ci-win2025-std-core-ja-jp-202608051603.x86-64, with the locale
    lowercased so the name remains a valid DNS label. Existing templates
    keep their old names; only new builds are affected.
  * pve-build-windows-template: record the locale and keyboard layout in
    the template description, which already listed the release, WIM image,
    source ISO and payload versions but not the language.

 -- Ciro Iriarte <ciro.iriarte+software@gmail.com>  Wed, 05 Aug 2026 19:30:00 -0300

pve-tools (1.12.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New tool:
    - pve-build-windows-template 1.3.0 - build sysprepped,
      Cloudbase-Init-capable Windows Server templates on PVE in one
      non-interactive run. Server 2019/2022/2025, Server Core and Desktop
      Experience (both by default, at consecutive VMIDs), Standard or
      Datacenter. UEFI/GPT on q35 + OVMF with TPM 2.0 and Secure Boot,
      virtio-scsi-single, virtio drivers injected into WinPE so Setup sees
      the disk. Installs the virtio driver set, QEMU guest agent, SPICE
      agent and Cloudbase-Init, enables RDP with its firewall rule, then
      syspreps and seals the template. Windows media is never downloaded
      unless --eval is passed; product keys and passwords are kept out of
      dry-run output, diagnostics and the remote process table. Local and
      remote (-S user@host) modes.
  * Any Windows Server localisation is supported. The built-in
    administrator and administrators group are resolved from their
    well-known SIDs rather than the English names, so --cipassword applies
    on media that localises them (Administrateur, Administrador). Generated
    in-guest scripts are asserted pure ASCII, because a non-ASCII byte is
    misread on a double-byte codepage such as GBK/936.
  * --eval covers the eight languages Microsoft publishes evaluation media
    in (en-US, fr-FR, es-ES, de-DE, it-IT, ja-JP, ru-RU, zh-CN). Media
    arriving in a language other than the one requested now fails the
    build: the Evaluation Center answers an unrecognised clcid with the
    English ISO and an HTTP 200, which would otherwise yield an English
    template labelled with another language.
  * The virtio driver versions are recorded after installation and
    re-checked once every later payload has run; a downgrade fails the
    build rather than silently shipping stale storage and network drivers.

 -- Ciro Iriarte <ciro.iriarte+software@gmail.com>  Wed, 05 Aug 2026 18:00:00 -0300

pve-tools (1.11.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * pve-sdn-healthcheck 1.2.0: add --parallel / SDN_PARALLEL (default 16) to
    scan nodes concurrently with a bounded worker pool. The per-node
    iface_errors drop-window sleep previously stacked serially (N nodes x
    SDN_DROP_WINDOW); fanning out keeps cluster-wide wall-time roughly flat
    as node count grows. Output is still buffered and reported in node order.

